/*!
    \class vsmm::IConfig
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Interface of the user settings, declares the properties \l vsmm::Config exposes to QML.

    IConfig is the abstract base of the user settings. It stores the three
    settings sections (\l vsmm::GeneralSettings, \l vsmm::PathSettings and
    \l vsmm::AppearanceSettings) and the list of favorite mod IDs in protected
    members, and returns them through its getters. Subclasses implement the
    section setters and \l validate().

    Other backend classes use a pointer to IConfig instead of
    \l vsmm::Config, so unit tests can pass a mock. \l vsmm::GameMngr connects
    to \l gameConfigPathChanged() and \l gameExePathChanged(), and
    \l vsmm::ModStore reads and writes the favorites through
    \l getFavorites() and \l setFavorites().

    \sa vsmm::Config
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::IConfig::CONFIG_FILE_NAME
    File name of the settings file, \c config.json.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::IConfig::FAVORITES_KEY_NAME
    JSON key of the favorite mod ID list in the settings file, \c favorites.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::IConfig::~IConfig()
    Destroys the object.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::IConfig::general
    \brief General behavior settings.

    \sa vsmm::GeneralSettings
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::IConfig::paths
    \brief Paths to the game data folder and the game executable.

    \sa vsmm::PathSettings
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::IConfig::appearance
    \brief Theme and accent color.

    \sa vsmm::AppearanceSettings
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::GeneralSettings vsmm::IConfig::general() const
    Returns the stored general settings.

    \sa setGeneral()
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::PathSettings vsmm::IConfig::paths() const
    Returns the stored path settings.

    \sa setPaths()
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::AppearanceSettings vsmm::IConfig::appearance() const
    Returns the stored appearance settings.

    \sa setAppearance()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IConfig::setGeneral(const vsmm::GeneralSettings &data)
    Replaces the general settings with \a data. Subclasses implement this.

    \sa general(), generalChanged()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IConfig::setPaths(const vsmm::PathSettings &data)
    Replaces the path settings with \a data. Subclasses implement this.

    \sa paths(), pathsChanged()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IConfig::setAppearance(const vsmm::AppearanceSettings &data)
    Replaces the appearance settings with \a data. Subclasses implement this.

    \sa appearance(), appearanceChanged()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IConfig::validate()
    Checks the loaded settings and emits the change signals for them.
    Subclasses implement this. \l vsmm::App calls it once after it connects
    the backend objects.
*/

/*!
    \fn const QStringList &vsmm::IConfig::getFavorites() const
    Returns the IDs of the favorite mods.

    \sa setFavorites()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IConfig::setFavorites(QStringList favorites)
    Replaces the IDs of the favorite mods with \a favorites. The base
    implementation only stores the list.

    \sa getFavorites()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IConfig::generalChanged()
    This signal is emitted when the \l general property changes.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IConfig::pathsChanged()
    This signal is emitted when the \l paths property changes.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IConfig::appearanceChanged()
    This signal is emitted when the \l appearance property changes.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IConfig::gameConfigPathChanged()
    This signal is emitted when the game data folder path
    (\l {vsmm::PathSettings::gameConfig}{PathSettings::gameConfig}) changes,
    and once by \l {vsmm::IConfig::validate()}{validate()}.
    \l vsmm::GameMngr connects to it to read the game client settings again.

    \sa gameExePathChanged()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IConfig::gameExePathChanged()
    This signal is emitted when the game executable path
    (\l {vsmm::PathSettings::gameExe}{PathSettings::gameExe}) changes.
    \l vsmm::GameMngr connects to it to read the game version again.

    \sa gameConfigPathChanged()
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::IConfig::mGeneral
    The stored general settings, returned by \l general().
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::IConfig::mPaths
    The stored path settings, returned by \l paths().
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::IConfig::mAppearance
    The stored appearance settings, returned by \l appearance().
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::IConfig::mFavorites
    The stored favorite mod IDs, returned by \l getFavorites().
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::Config
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief User settings stored in \c config.json.

    Config is the \l vsmm::IConfig implementation the app uses. It is
    registered as the QML singleton \c Config. The settings file is
    \c config.json inside the writable \c QStandardPaths::AppConfigLocation.

    The constructor creates the config directory if needed and reads the file
    when it exists and can be opened for reading and writing. A missing file, or a file whose top level is not a JSON
    object, leaves every section at its default values. A file that is not
    valid JSON stops the app with a fatal log message. Each section and the
    favorites list are read only when their key is present, and missing keys
    inside a section get the section defaults.

    The section setters do not save to disk. Call \l saveToFile() after a
    change, or rely on the destructor, which also saves:

    \code
    vsmm::PathSettings paths = config->paths();
    paths.gameConfig = QStringLiteral("/new/path");
    config->setPaths(paths);
    config->saveToFile();
    \endcode

    \l setFavorites() is the exception and saves the file right away.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::Config::Config()
    Creates the settings object and loads \c config.json if it exists.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::Config::~Config()
    Saves the settings to \c config.json and destroys the object.

    \sa saveToFile()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::Config::validate()
    \reimp
    Logs a critical message and emits nothing when the game data folder path
    is empty or the folder does not exist. Otherwise it emits
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::generalChanged()}{generalChanged()},
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::appearanceChanged()}{appearanceChanged()},
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::pathsChanged()}{pathsChanged()} and
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::gameConfigPathChanged()}{gameConfigPathChanged()}.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::Config::setFavorites(QStringList favorites)
    \reimp
    Also saves the settings file right away.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::Config::setGeneral(const vsmm::GeneralSettings &data)
    \reimp
    Does nothing when the value is equal to the stored one, otherwise emits
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::generalChanged()}{generalChanged()}.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::Config::setPaths(const vsmm::PathSettings &data)
    \reimp
    Does nothing when the value is equal to the stored one. Otherwise it emits
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::pathsChanged()}{pathsChanged()}, then
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::gameExePathChanged()}{gameExePathChanged()} and
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::gameConfigPathChanged()}{gameConfigPathChanged()} for
    the paths that differ.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::Config::setAppearance(const vsmm::AppearanceSettings &data)
    \reimp
    Does nothing when the value is equal to the stored one, otherwise emits
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::appearanceChanged()}{appearanceChanged()}.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::Config::saveToFile() const
    Writes the three settings sections and the favorite mod IDs to
    \c config.json as one JSON object. The write goes through \c QSaveFile, so
    the old file stays intact when writing fails. Failures are logged as
    warnings. QML can call this function.
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::GeneralSettings
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief General section of the user settings.

    GeneralSettings is a value type for the \c general section of
    \c config.json. Its members always have a value, and the defaults come
    from the \c DEFAULT_VALUE_ constants. \l fromHash() and \l toHash()
    convert the section to and from the JSON object that \l vsmm::Config reads
    and writes.

    QML sees this type as \c generalSettings, the type of
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::general}{Config.general}.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::GeneralSettings::KEY_NAME
    JSON key of this section in the settings file, \c general.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::GeneralSettings::DEFAULT_VALUE_DELETE_OLD_MOD_VERSION
    Default of \l deleteOldModVersion, \c true.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::GeneralSettings::DELETE_OLD_MOD_VERSION_KEY
    JSON key of \l deleteOldModVersion, \c deleteOldModVersion.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::GeneralSettings::DEFAULT_VALUE_INCLUDE_MOD_PRERELEASE
    Default of \l includeModPrerelease, \c false.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::GeneralSettings::INCLUDE_MOD_PRERELEASE_KEY
    JSON key of \l includeModPrerelease, \c includeModPrerelease.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::GeneralSettings::deleteOldModVersion
    Move the old zip to the trash when a mod is updated, by a download or by
    loading a newer zip of a known mod with the QML invokable \c load() of
    \l vsmm::ModLoader. A scan never deletes anything. Defaults to \c true.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::GeneralSettings::includeModPrerelease
    Consider pre-release versions when checking for updates. Defaults to
    \c false.
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::GeneralSettings::operator==(const vsmm::GeneralSettings &) const
    Returns \c true when every member equals the matching member of the
    other value.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::GeneralSettings vsmm::GeneralSettings::fromHash(const QVariantHash &hash)
    Returns the settings read from \a hash. A missing key gets its default
    value.

    \sa toHash()
*/

/*!
    \fn QVariantHash vsmm::GeneralSettings::toHash() const
    Returns the settings as a hash with one entry per member, keyed by the
    \c _KEY constants.

    \sa fromHash()
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::PathSettings
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Path section of the user settings.

    PathSettings is a value type for the \c paths section of \c config.json.
    Both paths are empty by default. \l fromHash() and \l toHash() convert the
    section to and from the JSON object that \l vsmm::Config reads and writes.

    QML sees this type as \c pathSettings, the type of
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::paths}{Config.paths}.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::PathSettings::KEY_NAME
    JSON key of this section in the settings file, \c paths.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::PathSettings::GAME_CONFIG_KEY
    JSON key of \l gameConfig, \c gameConfig.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::PathSettings::GAME_EXE_KEY
    JSON key of \l gameExe, \c gameExe.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::PathSettings::gameConfig
    The \c VintagestoryData folder. Empty by default.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::PathSettings::gameExe
    The Vintage Story executable. Empty by default.
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::PathSettings::operator==(const vsmm::PathSettings &) const
    Returns \c true when every member equals the matching member of the
    other value.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::PathSettings vsmm::PathSettings::fromHash(const QVariantHash &hash)
    Returns the settings read from \a hash. A missing key gives an empty path.

    \sa toHash()
*/

/*!
    \fn QVariantHash vsmm::PathSettings::toHash() const
    Returns the settings as a hash with one entry per member, keyed by the
    \c _KEY constants.

    \sa fromHash()
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::AppearanceSettings
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Appearance section of the user settings.

    AppearanceSettings is a value type for the \c appearance section of
    \c config.json. It stores the color theme and the index of the accent
    color. \l fromHash() and \l toHash() convert the section to and from the
    JSON object that \l vsmm::Config reads and writes. The file stores the
    theme as its lowercase name, see \l vsmm::themeToString() and
    \l vsmm::themeFromString().

    QML sees this type as \c appearanceSettings, the type of
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::appearance}{Config.appearance}.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::AppearanceSettings::KEY_NAME
    JSON key of this section in the settings file, \c appearance.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::AppearanceSettings::DEFAULT_VALUE_THEME
    Default of \l theme, \c {vsmm::appearance::Theme::Dark}.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::AppearanceSettings::THEME_KEY
    JSON key of \l theme, \c theme.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::AppearanceSettings::DEFAULT_VALUE_ACCENT_IDX
    Default of \l accentIndex, \c 0.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::AppearanceSettings::ACCENT_IDX_KEY
    JSON key of \l accentIndex, \c accentIndex.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::AppearanceSettings::theme
    The color theme. Defaults to \c Dark.

    \sa vsmm::appearance::Theme
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::AppearanceSettings::accentIndex
    Index of the accent color. Defaults to \c 0.
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::AppearanceSettings::operator==(const vsmm::AppearanceSettings &) const
    Returns \c true when every member equals the matching member of the
    other value.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::AppearanceSettings vsmm::AppearanceSettings::fromHash(const QVariantHash &hash)
    Returns the settings read from \a hash. The theme is parsed with
    \l vsmm::themeFromString(), so a missing or unknown theme name gives
    \c Dark. A missing accent index gives \c 0.

    \sa toHash()
*/

/*!
    \fn QVariantHash vsmm::AppearanceSettings::toHash() const
    Returns the settings as a hash with one entry per member, keyed by the
    \c _KEY constants. The theme is stored as the string from
    \l vsmm::themeToString().

    \sa fromHash()
*/

/*!
    \namespace vsmm::appearance
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Enums of the appearance settings.

    The namespace is registered with the meta-object system, so its enums are
    available to QML and to \c QMetaEnum.
*/

/*!
    \enum vsmm::appearance::Theme
    The color theme of the app.

    \value Dark Dark theme. This is the default.
    \value Light Light theme.

    \sa vsmm::AppearanceSettings::theme
*/

/*!
    \fn QString vsmm::themeToString(vsmm::appearance::Theme theme)
    \relates vsmm::AppearanceSettings
    Returns the enumerator name of \a theme in lowercase, for example
    \c dark.

    \sa themeFromString()
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::appearance::Theme vsmm::themeFromString(const QString &name)
    \relates vsmm::AppearanceSettings
    Returns the theme whose enumerator name matches \a name, ignoring case.
    Returns \c Dark when no name matches.

    \sa themeToString()
*/
